      "key": "openspec/changes/eutxo-compiler-correspondence/specs/eutxo-compiler/spec.md#EUC-001 Explicit factory and version routing",
      "id": "EUC-001",
      "group": "utxo-original",
      "clause": "WHEN source compilation selects financial agreement /5 or /6, the compiler SHALL derive Core with the matching source factory and bind /5 to expression contract /4 and lifecycle-state/1, and /6 to expression contract /5 and lifecycle-state/2. IF a requested profile, contract, lifecycle schema, or optional feature lacks an approved lowering table, THEN the compiler SHALL return a named unsupported diagnostic without a blueprint.",
      "source": {
        "path": "openspec/changes/eutxo-compiler-correspondence/specs/eutxo-compiler/spec.md",
        "sha256": "bbf910d7a5c006fe09b3d960817dabcce767927973a39046bf15ec8bd12b5bbe",
        "startLine": 3,
        "endLine": 13
      },
      "heading": "EUC-001 Explicit factory and version routing",
      "scenarios": [
        {
          "name": "Positive Compile the approved /5 custody source",
          "startLine": 6,
          "text": "- **WHEN** the source selects /5 and the scoped T1 capability\n- **THEN** the manifest records contract /4 and lifecycle-state/1",
          "scopeNote": "Verbatim span to next scenario or requirement. Final scenario may include following binding/acceptance prose; consult pinned source before atomization."
        },
        {
          "name": "Negative Prevent implicit profile migration",
          "startLine": 10,
          "text": "- **WHEN** a /6 source enters the T1-only compiler\n- **THEN** compilation refuses PROFILE_MISMATCH and produces no executable artifact",
          "scopeNote": "Verbatim span to next scenario or requirement. Final scenario may include following binding/acceptance prose; consult pinned source before atomization."
        }
      ],
